FINAL ANSWER:
**Bus factor: 1.** Troy Goode.

`lib/` is a single file, `lib/index.js` (238 lines, 67 commits, 25 authors).

Surviving lines by author, from `git blame -w -M -C`:

| Author | Lines | Share |
|---|---|---|
| Troy Goode | 138 | 58% |
| Fiona Formatter | 32 | 13% (the 2026-04-12 quote/indent reformat, so not real authorship) |
| Douglas Christopher Wilson | 18 | 8% |
| Alejandro Caravaca Puchades | 12 | 5% |
| Raymond Feng | 7 | 3% |
| 12 others | 31 | 13% |

- **Majority owner:** Troy alone holds over 50% of the lines. Without the formatter lines, Troy holds 138 of 206, or 67%.
- **Recent activity:** Only Troy has touched `lib/` in the last two years, apart from the formatter commit. Troy's last real commit is "lib: annotate handlers" on 2026-04-10.
- **Next contributor:** Douglas Christopher Wilson holds 8% of the lines. His last commit was 2017-10-04.
- **Everyone else:** The last commit from each other author is from 2021 or earlier. Most are one-off contributors with 1–3 lines left.

If Troy leaves, nobody active has written or recently changed this code.

Mitigating factors:
- The file is small, so a new maintainer can read all of it in under an hour.
- The file has had few changes recently.
- I did not check whether tests cover `lib/index.js`. If they do, that lowers the risk further. If they don't, it raises it.

To raise the bus factor, have a second person review or make real changes in `lib/index.js`. A reviewed PR would do. Reformat commits don't count.

