FINAL ANSWER:
**Bus factor of `lib/` is 1, measured by surviving lines.** That means the smallest number of authors whose surviving lines add up to 50% of the lines counted. It measures how concentrated the remaining code is. It does not measure who understands it.

`lib/` has only one file, with 238 surviving lines. All 238 were attributed, with no sampling.

| Author | Lines | Share | Commits | Share |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Troy Goode (2 addresses, merged) | 159 | 66.8% | 33 | 50.0% |
| Douglas Christopher Wilson | 22 | 9.2% | 4 | 6.1% |
| alex94puchades | 16 | 6.7% | 5 | 7.6% |
| Raymond Feng | 7 | 2.9% | 1 | 1.5% |
| LuisEGR | 6 | 2.5% | 1 | 1.5% |
| max.laverse | 6 | 2.5% | 1 | 1.5% |

14 more authors hold smaller shares.

- **Merge is a guess.** I counted `<email redacted>` and `troy@laptop.example` as one person because the name matches. Unmerged, `<email redacted>` holds 147 lines (61.8%) and the laptop address holds 12 (5.0%). The bus factor is 1 either way. I did not write a `.mailmap`, so nothing is permanent. Please confirm they are one person.
- **Bus factor at 80%:** 3 authors with the merge, or 4 without it. This is also for the `lib/` path only.
- **Reformat commit left out:** `62628c0` ("style: reformat js with 4-space indent and double quotes", Fiona Formatter) is excluded from the table. Counting it, Fiona Formatter would hold 32 lines (13.4%), and Troy Goode would hold 138 lines (58.0%) with the merge. The bus factor stays 1 either way.
- **Possible second duplicate:** the hint flagged `alex94puchades` as possibly the same person as "Alejandro Caravaca Puchades" (same address). The table shows only `alex94puchades`, with no merge applied, so that person may have more lines than shown.

If Troy leaves, 66.8% of the lines in `lib/` lose their author. Only Troy alone is above 50%, so the next four authors together hold less than Troy does. To cover 80% of the lines you would need Troy plus two more people, Wilson and one other.

These numbers say nothing about code quality, review work, or design discussion, and code that was deleted on purpose counts for nobody. Someone who reviewed or discussed this code may understand it well without owning any lines.

